Subject: [PATCH] mail: Keep just fetch from rewriting published mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: uxvxuvwrswokxpspsqtwmnsyxquvnlzv

just fetch rebases every ancestor of @ that claude@submissions lacks.
When the list has moved past the outbox Claude last pushed, those
ancestors include mail already pushed to upstream. jj refuses to
rewrite those immutable commits, and fetch fails until Claude
rebases and pushes again.

Rebase onto the newest of the published list and the outbox instead.
When the outbox is built on the list, as it usually is, that is
claude@submissions alone and the history stays linear. When the two
have diverged, @ becomes a merge of both, and no published commit is
rewritten.
---
change-id: uxvxuvwrswokxpspsqtwmnsyxquvnlzv

This applies to the mail line, not trunk: base-commit is mail@upstream.

Tested in a scratch repo with mail@origin immutable and Claude's
outbox on an untracked claude@submissions. With the outbox built on
the list, the old and new recipes agree and @ stays linear. With
Pat's pushed commit M not under the outbox, the old recipe fails with
"Commit ... is immutable", and the new one makes @ a merge of M and
the outbox.

 Justfile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Justfile b/Justfile
index 1e637a8..e0f32d0 100644
--- a/Justfile
+++ b/Justfile
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ advance:
 
 fetch:
   jj --quiet git fetch --remote submissions
-  jj --quiet rebase -b @ -d claude@submissions
+  jj --quiet rebase -b @ -d 'heads((::@ & immutable()) | claude@submissions)'
   jj --quiet simplify-parents
 
 push:

base-commit: 5c721a836a89d55db80627c81bca2c3cf4d7b976
